ackbar cycling forecast: no diagnostics, the restart set is the product
1900 1 1 0 0 0
#
# Line 2 is the FMS base date and ACKBAR rewrites it to the cycle's own start
# time, so the value committed here is never the one the model reads. It has to
# be a parseable date all the same, because this file is also what somebody
# reads to see what a cycling forecast writes.
#
# Nothing below it on purpose. A cycling forecast exists to hand a state to the
# next cycle, and at one degree with an ensemble the history it would otherwise
# write every cycle is larger than the restarts and is read by nothing. Anything
# that wants fields off the background reads the restart set, and an experiment
# that wants model history configures an extended forecast, whose whole reason
# for existing is to be scored.
